A||||7||ezsurf||Diagonistic Tools||||
Z||000000||ezsurf||08-16-99||09:03 PM||||<br>Can a laptop computer be hooked up to the diagonistic terminal on the Fiero, or do you have to have a code reader?  If a laptop can be attached, does anyone who makes the diagonistic software and adapter plug?
Z||000001||theogre||08-16-99||10:05 PM||||yes, you can hook a PC to an ECM. It's almost as expensive time& material wise as buying a good scanner.<p>A "code reader" is just that. It reads ECM codes. you can do that much for free via the light on the dash.<p>An ECM "scanner" reads not only codes but the real time data from the ECM as well. (For an 87 4 cyl that means 40+ seperate outputs, including the cruise control settings) The AutoXray GM only scanner is about 150$us complete with cable.
Z||000002||ezsurf||08-16-99||10:21 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I thought it would be nice if I could get a $50 program to run on my $2000 laptop rather than spend $150+ on an ECM scanner.  I don't know why I thought something on this car could be simple.
Z||000003||terryk||08-17-99||12:21 AM||||Diacom from Rinda Technologies is damn good for the price. $250 and runs on a laptop. You can log runs and other things. Connects to the parallel port and the ALDL connector.
Z||000004||terryk||08-17-99||12:22 AM||||Diacom from Rinda Technologies is damn good for the price. $250 and runs on a laptop. You can log runs and other things. Connects to the parallel port and the ALDL connector.
Z||000005||ezsurf||08-17-99||10:08 PM||||Ogre,<br>I'm guessing your scanner is an Auto XRAY XP240.  Where did you find it for $150, and would you say this scanner is worth it?
Z||000006||theogre||08-18-99||08:04 AM||||It's the GM only one what ever number it is I don't know. It covers 82-95 GM cars, and includes the cable. XP240 is the universal one, it's 250 Plus the cables at $30 each.<p>Eastwood carries them  <A HREF="http://www.eastwoodco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.eastwoodco.com</A>  the GM only one thru them is 190$us. I got mine from Strauss Discount auto, a local/regional dealer, for $149.<p>Yes, it's worth it. I've used it for several things, including confirming proper operation when I put a 180 thermostat in. On my 87 it can track over 40 functions, including the cruise controll. It won't do the cruise on cars like pre 87 4 cyls that use seperate brains for the cruise.
Z||000007||Mark||10-21-1999||07:32 PM||||Has anyone tried the "new" ALDL PC Interface software by Frans Godshalk (on the Fiero-Tech-Zone website)?  For $15, it seem like just what the doctor ordered...that is, if it works.||||reg||5
